[65.5509, "o", "  glimmer-30b — 30 tool call(s) so far\r\n  ⚙ todo \r\n    ✓ todo — 2/4 done · Diagnose pip install failure\r\n  ⚙ todo \r\n    ✓ todo — 3/4 done · Fix issue\r\n[approval] bash: python3 -m pip list — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash python3 -m pip list\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  glimmer-30b — 31 tool call(s) so far\r\n  glimmer-30b — 32 tool call(s) so far\r\n  ⚙ note \r\n    ✓ note — pip dist-info existed without pip package files; ensurepip t\r\n  [tools] 32/256 calls — continuing (leg 2)\r\n  glimmer-30b — leg 2, 32 call(s) so far\r\n  glimmer-30b — 33 tool call(s) so far\r\n  ⚙ todo \r\n    ✓ todo — 4/4 done\r\nThe system-wide Python 3.13 installation had a broken pip: `/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip-24.3.1.dist-info` existed but the actual `pip` package directory was missing, so `pip3` raised `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'pip'`. `ensurepip` considered pip “already satisfied” because the dist-info was present.\r\n\r\nFixed by removing the stale metadata and re-bootstrapping pip from"]
[65.550982, "o", " the bundled wheel:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nrm -rf /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip-24.3.1.dist-info\r\npython3 -m ensurepip --default-pip\r\n```\r\n\r\nVerification:\r\n```\r\n$ python3 -m pip --version\r\npip 24.3.1 from /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip (python 3.13)\r\n\r\n$ python3 -m pip list\r\nPackage Version\r\n------- -------\r\npip     24.3.1\r\n```\r\n\r\n`pip` now imports and runs correctly. Network is disabled in this sandbox, so remote installs can’t be tested here, but the bootstrap is complete and `python3 -m pip` works end-to-end.\r\n\r\n[refusal] role=implementor model=glimmer-30b tools=33 surface=305ca09d0222\r\n"]
